# `main` cannot return a status, and diff(1)-style tools need 0/1/2. The message
# must name `exit(code)`, which is the shape that CAN express it and which five
# programs under tools/ already use -- naming only Result(void, string) sends the
# reader to redesign around two outcomes. Found writing tools/tycho-diff.
fn main() -> int:
    return 2
